1
00:00:01,418 --> 00:00:03,629
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:31,675 --> 00:01:32,926
[indistinct chatter]

3
00:01:38,557 --> 00:01:40,267
-[door opens]
-Ah, good day to you.

4
00:01:41,018 --> 00:01:44,104
Oh. Well that is not
who I was expecting to see.

5
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:46,606
[MAOMAO] You're not as bad
as fox face, but you're close.

6
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:48,900
Your manners are
as atrocious as ever.

7
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:56,283
[MAOMAO] This is Lahan.

8
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:59,828
As made obvious by his name,
he's a member of the La clan.

9
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:03,123
He's also the freak strategist's
nephew and adopted son.

10
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:06,084
I didn't know
you were interested in shows.

11
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:09,212
[LAHAN] When it feels like
all the world's interested,

12
00:02:09,296 --> 00:02:10,964
how can I not be intrigued?

13
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:14,343
Huh? Hmm.

14
00:02:14,426 --> 00:02:16,636
Then there's
this albino princess.

15
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,722
Reports indicate
she's very beautiful.

16
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:20,557
[MAOMAO] Oh, I forgot.

17
00:02:20,641 --> 00:02:23,101
This guy's obsessed
with aesthetics.

18
00:02:23,185 --> 00:02:26,021
But unlike most people,
he breaks it down into numbers.

19
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:29,775
Like father, like adoptive son.

20
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:33,070
So the purpose of your visit
is to invite me along.

21
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:35,155
Admit it, you're curious too.

22
00:02:35,614 --> 00:02:36,698
I won't deny it.

23
00:02:37,324 --> 00:02:40,410
But I don't see how asking me
to come along benefits him.

24
00:02:40,494 --> 00:02:42,496
Probably trying
to score weirdo points

25
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:44,373
with the weirdo strategist.

26
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:45,874
[LAHAN]
Father didn't accompany me.

27
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:47,042
[MAOMAO] Peculiar.

28
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:48,585
[LAHAN]
His subordinate did, though.

29
00:02:48,668 --> 00:02:49,628
[Rikuson chuckles]

30
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:50,921
[groans]

31
00:02:51,213 --> 00:02:53,382
[RIKUSON] What is with
that look? I'm Master Lakan's--

32
00:02:53,465 --> 00:02:54,841
-Hmm?
-[Maomao growls]

33
00:02:54,925 --> 00:02:55,801
[clears throat]

34
00:02:56,677 --> 00:02:57,886
My mistake.

35
00:02:57,969 --> 00:02:59,930
Perhaps I shouldn't use
his name around you.

36
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:00,972
Uh.

37
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:04,768
I'm the master strategist's
subordinate, Rikuson.

38
00:03:05,519 --> 00:03:06,561
I'm Maomao.

39
00:03:07,187 --> 00:03:08,563
It's an honor to meet you.

40
00:03:09,314 --> 00:03:11,691
Why did he send his men,
and not come himself?

41
00:03:12,818 --> 00:03:16,154
[LAHAN] Father probably won't be
leaving the mansion for a while.

42
00:03:17,322 --> 00:03:18,907
Huh. Still, though,

43
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:20,450
why do you care if I go?

44
00:03:21,451 --> 00:03:22,744
Lahan wouldn't invite me

45
00:03:22,828 --> 00:03:24,746
unless there was something in it
for him.

46
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:26,998
To my knowledge, he's a miser,

47
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:29,251
on par with the old lady.

48
00:03:29,793 --> 00:03:32,379
You see, he has some dealing
with the west coming up.

49
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:34,923
We were thinking of asking
that traveling performer

50
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:37,342
and her troupe to do
a little show at a party.

51
00:03:37,676 --> 00:03:38,635
Go on.

52
00:03:39,261 --> 00:03:41,721
And since there will be women
among the delegation too,

53
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:44,349
I was wanting to get
a feminine perspective as well.

54
00:03:44,433 --> 00:03:46,309
-Liar.
-[chuckles]

55
00:03:47,394 --> 00:03:49,146
[MAOMAO]
What an annoying gesture.

56
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:50,730
In truth,

57
00:03:50,814 --> 00:03:51,732
earlier,

58
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:54,526
the master strategist
had this to say about her.

59
00:03:56,403 --> 00:03:57,779
I find it concerning.

60
00:03:57,863 --> 00:03:59,322
[piece clacks]

61
00:03:59,406 --> 00:04:01,241
But that's all he said.

62
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,409
[MAOMAO]
It's not out of character

63
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:04,703
for him to make
cryptic passing remarks.

64
00:04:04,786 --> 00:04:07,706
Although, he has an almost
supernatural intuition.

65
00:04:07,789 --> 00:04:11,209
Furthermore, we looked
into all of the performers.

66
00:04:11,293 --> 00:04:14,212
It seems hushed whispers
follow them around.

67
00:04:14,296 --> 00:04:15,380
Rumors?

68
00:04:15,464 --> 00:04:16,506
Yes.

69
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:19,468
♪

70
00:04:23,555 --> 00:04:25,849
[MAOMAO] Hopefully,
there's no trouble tonight.

71
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:31,062
Shall we be off?

72
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:32,689
[horse trotting]

73
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:38,779
[MAOMAO] Of all the venues,

74
00:04:39,154 --> 00:04:41,239
she chose a theater
in the richest part of the city.

75
00:04:42,073 --> 00:04:44,534
Near a high-class
residential area,

76
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:46,786
she performs a solo show.

77
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:48,246
How bizarre.

78
00:04:48,788 --> 00:04:51,208
The sorceress is referred to
as "The White Lady"

79
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:52,501
due to her looks,

80
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:54,961
and is worshiped like a goddess.

81
00:04:55,045 --> 00:04:57,672
It's quite an achievement
for a traveling performer.

82
00:04:58,548 --> 00:05:01,009
Seems so worldly
for a sorceress.

83
00:05:02,093 --> 00:05:03,178
-[LAHAN] We're here.
-Huh?

84
00:05:03,261 --> 00:05:05,680
[guests chattering]

85
00:05:07,849 --> 00:05:08,725
[coins jangle]

86
00:05:08,808 --> 00:05:09,810
[SERVANT] Thank you.

87
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:11,394
[MAOMAO] What is this?

88
00:05:11,770 --> 00:05:14,105
[LAHAN] Like you said,
it's all very worldly.

89
00:05:14,481 --> 00:05:16,858
Sometimes, it can be
advantageous to have pretext

90
00:05:16,942 --> 00:05:19,194
for claiming you don't
recognize anyone else.

91
00:05:19,277 --> 00:05:20,237
[Maomao groans]

92
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:28,411
A traveling solo performer
working at a theater this large?

93
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:30,372
She must have a sponsor.

94
00:05:30,914 --> 00:05:32,499
Looks like our table
is over there.

95
00:05:35,377 --> 00:05:36,628
[LAHAN] Oh?

96
00:05:37,379 --> 00:05:39,839
[BASEN] You really didn't need
to bother yourself with this.

97
00:05:40,382 --> 00:05:41,299
[JINSHI] It's fine.

98
00:05:41,383 --> 00:05:42,926
And a rare opportunity.

99
00:05:43,009 --> 00:05:43,885
[BASEN] Even so.

100
00:05:44,636 --> 00:05:47,389
[JINSHI] I want to see this
"White Lady" with my own eyes.

101
00:05:48,682 --> 00:05:50,141
[RIKUSON] This must be us.

102
00:05:50,225 --> 00:05:51,977
[LAHAN] The center seats
are quite popular.

103
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:54,271
They've hiked the price way up.

104
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:56,106
[laughter]

105
00:05:56,189 --> 00:05:58,692
-Don't you genuinely think so?
-[all laugh]

106
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:00,402
Please enjoy yourselves.

107
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:04,322
[MAOMAO] Baked snacks
to go along with the alcohol?

108
00:06:04,406 --> 00:06:06,616
What a strange combination.

109
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:10,078
[sniffs]

110
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:12,330
[LAHAN] It's alcohol.
Not going to drink?

111
00:06:12,956 --> 00:06:14,291
[MAOMAO] I do love booze, but...

112
00:06:15,166 --> 00:06:16,543
I'll have some later.

113
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:18,878
Or are you waiting
for me to check it for poison?

114
00:06:19,296 --> 00:06:20,630
[LAHAN] How kind, but no.

115
00:06:20,714 --> 00:06:22,173
[MAOMAO]
You're not drinking either?

116
00:06:22,257 --> 00:06:24,134
I can't afford
to be the only one

117
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:25,552
making blunders tonight.

118
00:06:25,635 --> 00:06:27,679
Huh. These go well together.

119
00:06:27,762 --> 00:06:29,264
They have a unique taste.

120
00:06:34,019 --> 00:06:35,020
[gong crashes]

121
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:37,689
Uh.

122
00:06:39,149 --> 00:06:41,067
[♪ mysterious music playing]

123
00:06:41,151 --> 00:06:43,069
[footsteps]

124
00:06:53,288 --> 00:06:54,331
[both gasp]

125
00:06:54,414 --> 00:06:56,541
[hushed chatter]

126
00:06:56,625 --> 00:06:58,752
[MAOMAO] It's her.
The White Lady.

127
00:06:59,586 --> 00:07:00,920
[JINSHI] Her appearance aside,

128
00:07:01,004 --> 00:07:03,214
something about her
seems foreign.

129
00:07:03,298 --> 00:07:04,424
Is she from the west?

130
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:13,099
[gong crashes]

131
00:07:18,647 --> 00:07:21,650
[ASSISTANT] May we please have
a volunteer from this table?

132
00:07:22,317 --> 00:07:24,903
-[Lahan gasps] That's our table.
-Well, lucky us.

133
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:26,154
[LAHAN] What should we do?

134
00:07:26,237 --> 00:07:28,406
That is hardly
a question for me.

135
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:30,450
[LAHAN]
Why don't you go in our place?

136
00:07:30,992 --> 00:07:32,661
You'll get to see
the act up close.

137
00:07:33,495 --> 00:07:34,496
Hmm.

138
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:36,915
Fine, I'll volunteer.

139
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:39,626
[JINSHI] Huh?

140
00:07:40,043 --> 00:07:40,961
Is that...

141
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:47,509
No. It can't be.

142
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:54,766
[MAOMAO] I can see her veins
through her skin.

143
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:57,727
Her paleness isn't just
from cosmetics.

144
00:07:58,353 --> 00:08:01,231
Please write any number
you would like on the paper.

145
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:02,816
[ASSISTANT]
"Please write any number

146
00:08:02,899 --> 00:08:04,442
you would like on the paper!"

147
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:10,156
Be sure I'm unable to see
what you've written.

148
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:12,200
Then fold the paper very small

149
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:14,619
so that no one else
can observe it.

150
00:08:21,710 --> 00:08:23,545
[MAOMAO]
I guess she means on this.

151
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:25,714
They even have
a board to make sure

152
00:08:25,797 --> 00:08:27,549
the paper doesn't stick
to the table.

153
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:29,050
Hmm?

154
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:32,011
This brush holds a lot of ink.

155
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:34,514
It's hard to write.

156
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:36,933
The liquid has a grain to it.

157
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:38,685
Don't they know
how to mix ink properly?

158
00:08:42,439 --> 00:08:43,565
I'm finished.

159
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,115
If you'd be so kind,

160
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:55,285
place the paper inside
one of these openings.

161
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:56,536
Once you're finished,

162
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:58,747
please cover it up
with the cloth.

163
00:09:07,047 --> 00:09:07,964
[MAOMAO] Done.

164
00:09:17,182 --> 00:09:18,683
-[gong crashes]
-[gasps]

165
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:36,326
[jingles]

166
00:09:38,953 --> 00:09:42,290
So, the White Lady
has poor eyesight.

167
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:44,375
[WHITE LADY] The number
you wrote on the parchment,

168
00:09:44,459 --> 00:09:46,669
-it was seven.
-[Maomao gasps]

169
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:48,713
-[bell jingles]
-[gong crashes]

170
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:51,341
Am I right?

171
00:09:55,345 --> 00:09:56,429
[MAOMAO] Her eyes.

172
00:09:56,513 --> 00:09:58,848
She's like a white snake.

173
00:10:00,642 --> 00:10:03,311
You shouldn't kill
a servant to the gods.

174
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:06,439
[MAOMAO] Gods have nothing
to do with anything.

175
00:10:07,732 --> 00:10:10,819
But sometimes, Dad would pull
weird morals out of nowhere.

176
00:10:12,237 --> 00:10:14,364
Why is it so hot on stage?

177
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:15,698
And my head hurts.

178
00:10:16,699 --> 00:10:19,661
It's like a mosquito is
buzzing around my ear.

179
00:10:22,914 --> 00:10:24,582
The tube you placed the paper,

180
00:10:25,083 --> 00:10:28,586
it was three from the top
and two from the left.

181
00:10:32,215 --> 00:10:33,258
Am I correct?

182
00:10:38,304 --> 00:10:40,849
[ASSISTANT] Third from the top
and two from the left!

183
00:10:40,932 --> 00:10:42,016
Watch carefully.

184
00:10:45,353 --> 00:10:48,022
[impressed chatter]

185
00:10:48,106 --> 00:10:49,732
[ASSISTANT]
She has written "seven."

186
00:10:49,816 --> 00:10:51,401
How'd she know the number?

187
00:10:51,484 --> 00:10:53,069
And she guessed
the exact location!

188
00:10:53,153 --> 00:10:54,279
[applause]

189
00:10:54,362 --> 00:10:55,864
But that shouldn't be possible.

190
00:10:57,657 --> 00:10:59,325
[JINSHI] If anyone could
figure out her trick,

191
00:10:59,409 --> 00:11:00,869
it would surely be Maomao.

192
00:11:02,162 --> 00:11:03,913
[LAHAN] What exactly
happened up there?

193
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:06,249
What do you mean, what?

194
00:11:06,708 --> 00:11:09,711
[LAHAN] I mean, did they pay you
off to help them or something?

195
00:11:10,295 --> 00:11:11,921
Please. I am not like you.

196
00:11:12,005 --> 00:11:13,590
[LAHAN] As if I would
stoop so low.

197
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:15,842
-There'd be no beauty in it.
-[chuckles]

198
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:17,635
[LAHAN]
Did anyone see what you did?

199
00:11:17,719 --> 00:11:20,263
I don't think it has anything
to do with seeing.

200
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:22,891
Only the White Lady
and her assistant

201
00:11:22,974 --> 00:11:24,225
were on the stage.

202
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:26,978
They weren't able
to view anything.

203
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:28,479
Not to mention,

204
00:11:28,563 --> 00:11:31,357
I put the cloth on top
of the tube, concealing it.

205
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:34,527
Perhaps if there was a mirror...

206
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:39,365
No. There was too much haze
in the air, and little light.

207
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:41,201
The reflection
would be obscured.

208
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:45,163
Besides, the White Lady
seems to have poor vision.

209
00:11:45,246 --> 00:11:47,206
Everything
must be blurry for her,

210
00:11:47,290 --> 00:11:49,626
even at relatively
short distances.

211
00:11:51,044 --> 00:11:52,962
♪

212
00:11:56,299 --> 00:11:58,217
It's a piece of copper.

213
00:11:58,301 --> 00:11:59,594
Nothing all that special.

214
00:12:04,057 --> 00:12:06,226
[whispering] What once
lied beneath, let emerge.

215
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:23,326
[guests chuckling, chattering]

216
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:28,623
[MAOMAO]
It became a different color.

217
00:12:28,706 --> 00:12:30,625
[GUEST 1] She changed it
from copper to silver!

218
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:31,918
[GUEST 2] Show me how it's done!

219
00:12:32,001 --> 00:12:33,461
[GUEST 3]
I can't believe my eyes!

220
00:12:43,805 --> 00:12:44,889
[guests gasp]

221
00:12:44,973 --> 00:12:46,224
[GUEST 4] The silver
turned into gold!

222
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:47,809
That's impossible!

223
00:12:48,268 --> 00:12:51,354
-[JINSHI] Basen.
-Uh, right. My apologies.

224
00:12:54,565 --> 00:12:56,234
[LAHAN] Can you explain
what just occurred?

225
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:57,402
Afterwards.

226
00:12:58,027 --> 00:12:59,821
For now,
I want to enjoy the show.

227
00:13:00,947 --> 00:13:02,824
Ignite what was once dormant.

228
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:06,744
[whispering]
Reveal your inferno to us.

229
00:13:08,121 --> 00:13:09,539
[guests gasp]

230
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:16,796
[excited chatter]

231
00:13:21,843 --> 00:13:23,344
[guests gasp]

232
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:28,307
[GUEST 5] Silver-colored liquid?

233
00:13:28,391 --> 00:13:29,809
[GUEST 6]
What do you think it is?

234
00:13:32,312 --> 00:13:33,896
Is that... Can't be.

235
00:13:36,691 --> 00:13:37,817
[gulps]

236
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:40,069
[gasps]

237
00:13:40,695 --> 00:13:43,364
I certainly hope you enjoyed
my show this evening.

238
00:13:44,032 --> 00:13:45,992
I hope to see you again.

239
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:47,785
-[applause]
-What wonderful sorcery!

240
00:13:47,869 --> 00:13:49,412
This girl's the real deal!

241
00:13:49,495 --> 00:13:52,040
My muse! Teach me your ways!

242
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,542
So did we see actual sorcery?

243
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:56,586
[JINSHI] There must be
some kind of trick.

244
00:13:57,420 --> 00:13:58,421
We're leaving.

245
00:13:58,504 --> 00:13:59,505
Sir.

246
00:14:00,256 --> 00:14:01,674
[JINSHI] Look into
high-ranking officials

247
00:14:01,758 --> 00:14:02,842
frequenting this place.

248
00:14:03,593 --> 00:14:04,469
Right.

249
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:06,679
[JINSHI] The White Lady.

250
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:08,222
She's dangerous.

251
00:14:13,644 --> 00:14:15,480
A strange feeling
has washed over me.

252
00:14:17,774 --> 00:14:20,151
-Is there something wrong?
-Indeed.

253
00:14:26,824 --> 00:14:28,785
-There's an added substance.
-[MAN] Huh?

254
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:31,204
[sniffs]

255
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:33,206
The alcohol isn't very strong.

256
00:14:33,289 --> 00:14:35,374
It's easy to drink,
like a fruit juice.

257
00:14:35,458 --> 00:14:37,043
But there's a faint twist.

258
00:14:37,668 --> 00:14:39,712
Salt's been introduced
into the beverage.

259
00:14:40,213 --> 00:14:41,714
While it's not a poison,

260
00:14:41,798 --> 00:14:44,384
it's been mixed in to make
the alcohol much stronger.

261
00:14:45,343 --> 00:14:46,552
Also...

262
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:48,679
The dark room,

263
00:14:48,763 --> 00:14:50,932
combined
with the flickering lamps.

264
00:14:51,015 --> 00:14:52,683
Plus, the mysterious haze,

265
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:54,769
and a fantastic sorceress.

266
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:57,855
We've been inundated
with the strange and new.

267
00:14:57,939 --> 00:14:59,524
Seems like
there's more than enough

268
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:01,109
to convince someone
to worship blindly.

269
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:04,570
It's not a terrible flavor,

270
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:06,447
but it could do
without the salt.

271
00:15:06,531 --> 00:15:07,782
[gasps]

272
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:12,829
[LAHAN] What are you doing?

273
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:14,664
So that's what's going on.

274
00:15:15,248 --> 00:15:16,666
If they're using trickery here,

275
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:18,751
something similar
must've happened up there.

276
00:15:19,502 --> 00:15:21,337
The haze was thicker
on the stage.

277
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:24,382
Not to mention, it was hotter
and headache-inducing.

278
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:26,801
That made it hard
for me to concentrate.

279
00:15:27,218 --> 00:15:30,304
What if
it was some sort of vapor?

280
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:33,641
They could have been pumping
steam in from behind the stage.

281
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:35,893
Which would explain the heat.

282
00:15:35,977 --> 00:15:38,396
But what about the headache
I experienced?

283
00:15:38,980 --> 00:15:41,190
I heard a buzzing
like a mosquito.

284
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:43,192
Could it be...

285
00:15:43,818 --> 00:15:44,902
Mm?

286
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:49,282
[whistles softly]

287
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:50,992
[LAHAN] I hope you're not trying
to taunt them.

288
00:15:51,659 --> 00:15:53,411
Really, that is beneath you.

289
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:55,580
-[continues whistling]
-[LAHAN] Uh.

290
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:58,624
-[continues whistling]
-[White Lady gasps]

291
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:01,210
[MAOMAO] Ah. I get it now.

292
00:16:01,794 --> 00:16:04,714
[indistinct chatter]

293
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:08,134
[giggles]

294
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:09,886
Booze tastes so much better

295
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:11,220
when you're not
the one paying for it!

296
00:16:11,846 --> 00:16:13,639
Strange you don't get
invited out more.

297
00:16:13,723 --> 00:16:15,808
[MAOMAO] Please.
Your family can afford it.

298
00:16:15,892 --> 00:16:17,393
We made quite
a significant purchase

299
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:19,061
from the Verdigris House
last year.

300
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:20,771
So, we are practically broke.

301
00:16:20,855 --> 00:16:23,608
Now that we're somewhere safe,
can you tell us what you know?

302
00:16:24,192 --> 00:16:25,151
First off,

303
00:16:25,610 --> 00:16:27,778
turning copper into silver
and gold is nothing new.

304
00:16:27,862 --> 00:16:28,863
The practice is similar

305
00:16:28,946 --> 00:16:30,740
to something
called transmutation.

306
00:16:30,823 --> 00:16:32,241
[RIKUSON] Transmutation?

307
00:16:32,325 --> 00:16:35,745
Or perhaps you're familiar
with the term "liandan-shu."

308
00:16:36,454 --> 00:16:38,956
Transmutation,
converting non-metal to metal,

309
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:41,042
is a subcategory
of the practice.

310
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:42,960
So that's what we saw on stage?

311
00:16:43,044 --> 00:16:46,047
Yes, but from my limited
knowledge on the matter,

312
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:47,590
I would say
it more closely resembled

313
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:49,467
the practice of "alchemy"
from the west.

314
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:51,093
[LAHAN] Far from us, then.

315
00:16:51,177 --> 00:16:53,596
Yeah. I only heard about it
from my dad.

316
00:16:54,764 --> 00:16:56,557
Before you get too excited,

317
00:16:56,641 --> 00:16:58,684
it doesn't actually
turn silver into gold.

318
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:01,646
Material is plated
and exposed to fire

319
00:17:01,729 --> 00:17:04,273
to give the appearance
of changing into something else.

320
00:17:05,233 --> 00:17:07,860
And by "plated,"
what is it you mean?

321
00:17:07,944 --> 00:17:09,487
You would take your base metal,

322
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:11,531
then apply a thinner metal
on top of it.

323
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:14,450
If you want more details,
you can ask my dad.

324
00:17:14,534 --> 00:17:16,369
And afterwards, it'd be great
if you could tell me

325
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:17,620
what information he shared.

326
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:20,540
-In fact, do that.
-[Lahan spluttering]

327
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:23,626
[MAOMAO] As for the moment where
the paper burned on its own,

328
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:26,963
the byproducts of the process
are enough to cause combustion.

329
00:17:27,672 --> 00:17:29,924
The butterflies that appeared
could simply be an effect

330
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:31,676
of using high-class paper.

331
00:17:32,552 --> 00:17:33,594
Furthermore,

332
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:36,389
with the addition of the haze
and the intoxicating drink,

333
00:17:36,472 --> 00:17:38,766
the audience's vision
would have been impaired.

334
00:17:39,475 --> 00:17:40,851
You didn't drink, Lahan,

335
00:17:40,935 --> 00:17:42,728
and even you were tricked
by the illusion.

336
00:17:42,812 --> 00:17:44,355
It was executed perfectly.

337
00:17:45,106 --> 00:17:46,899
All right.
So, what about the moment

338
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:47,984
she saw through your mind?

339
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:50,444
That is the interesting part.

340
00:17:52,405 --> 00:17:53,614
Paper.

341
00:17:53,698 --> 00:17:55,074
[LAHAN] You could say please.

342
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:05,209
The wet part
seems to be shrinking.

343
00:18:05,668 --> 00:18:06,794
[MAOMAO]
Look at the bigger picture.

344
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:09,880
[scoffs] Can't you show respect
to your elder brother?

345
00:18:09,964 --> 00:18:11,257
[MAOMAO] Never gonna happen.

346
00:18:12,049 --> 00:18:13,301
[RIKUSON] I'm afraid I don't see

347
00:18:13,384 --> 00:18:15,469
how this connects
to the performance.

348
00:18:16,679 --> 00:18:17,722
[MAOMAO] Watch closely.

349
00:18:20,891 --> 00:18:21,851
[both gasp]

350
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:23,561
[MAOMAO]
I've used the same trick,

351
00:18:23,644 --> 00:18:25,104
revealing writing through heat.

352
00:18:25,187 --> 00:18:26,939
Master Jinshi
would have figured it out

353
00:18:27,023 --> 00:18:28,024
without the demonstration.

354
00:18:28,691 --> 00:18:29,567
Well?

355
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:30,901
What do you mean by "well"?

356
00:18:30,985 --> 00:18:32,695
I don't understand
how what you just showed us

357
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:34,739
has anything to do
with reading--

358
00:18:35,656 --> 00:18:36,657
How's it taste?

359
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:39,285
Mm. It's a seafood broth,
so the flavor's good.

360
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:40,619
But a wee bit salty.

361
00:18:40,703 --> 00:18:42,413
Again, we have
the presence of salt.

362
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:43,497
Why does that matter?

363
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:46,375
[MAOMAO] The ink on the brush
had salt in it too.

364
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:50,129
It's no wonder it was grainy
and difficult to write with.

365
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:52,840
She burned the paper
to read the number?

366
00:18:52,923 --> 00:18:55,051
No.
They utilized another method.

367
00:18:56,093 --> 00:18:58,387
There was a dark board
underneath where I wrote.

368
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:01,724
The salty ink went through
the paper and seeped into it.

369
00:19:02,350 --> 00:19:03,893
[LAHAN] So that's how.

370
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:05,144
[RIKUSON] I see.

371
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:06,520
[LAHAN] All right then.

372
00:19:06,604 --> 00:19:08,147
How did she know
the precise tube

373
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:09,523
that contained the paper?

374
00:19:11,650 --> 00:19:14,111
You understand
how a flute works, right?

375
00:19:15,071 --> 00:19:16,781
[LAHAN]
Blowing air creates a sound.

376
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:19,492
[squeaks]

377
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:21,327
And to change the sound?

378
00:19:21,410 --> 00:19:24,580
Simply alter the number
of holes the air blows through.

379
00:19:24,664 --> 00:19:26,248
Even I am aware of that much.

380
00:19:26,916 --> 00:19:29,001
[MAOMAO] So, what if the tubes
with the paper

381
00:19:29,085 --> 00:19:31,712
worked in a similar way,
like holes in a flute?

382
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:34,465
[LAHAN] Wait.
But I didn't hear anything.

383
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:36,926
[MAOMAO] In that theater,

384
00:19:37,009 --> 00:19:39,261
there was one other
important sound.

385
00:19:39,345 --> 00:19:41,514
Hidden behind
the bells and gongs.

386
00:19:42,598 --> 00:19:44,475
It would have been
quite high-pitched,

387
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:46,143
almost unnoticeable.

388
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:47,895
How high-pitched?

389
00:19:47,978 --> 00:19:48,896
[MAOMAO] Very.

390
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:51,649
A pitch that causes headaches
at certain ranges.

391
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:53,484
It might not register
as a sound,

392
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:56,362
but it can still
cause discomfort unconsciously.

393
00:19:56,445 --> 00:19:57,571
[inhales]

394
00:19:57,655 --> 00:19:59,865
-[whistles]
-I can hear that.

395
00:19:59,949 --> 00:20:00,866
[MAOMAO] How about this?

396
00:20:01,742 --> 00:20:02,785
[high-pitched whistle]

397
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:04,078
I hear that too.

398
00:20:04,704 --> 00:20:06,247
It's difficult for me.

399
00:20:06,831 --> 00:20:08,290
Hmm. I heard nothing.

400
00:20:08,874 --> 00:20:10,543
[MAOMAO]
And that would make sense.

401
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:12,920
Hearing gets harder
the older you get.

402
00:20:13,003 --> 00:20:14,046
[gasps]

403
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:16,298
[MAOMAO]
And I noticed the sorceress

404
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:17,800
was extremely sensitive.

405
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:21,220
So, she was able to use
the pitch of the flute

406
00:20:21,303 --> 00:20:22,763
to figure out
which tube the paper was in?

407
00:20:22,847 --> 00:20:27,518
Yes. The gong and bells simply
acted as cues to blow air.

408
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:29,645
She'd need to differentiate
around 10 sounds

409
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:30,771
to make it work.

410
00:20:30,855 --> 00:20:32,314
[LAHAN]
But how would one "blow air"?

411
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:35,234
[MAOMAO] The haze was doing
more than setting the mood.

412
00:20:35,317 --> 00:20:36,694
[liquid boiling]

413
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:37,736
It was a vapor.

414
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,280
Probably steam being pushed

415
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:41,073
through the lower part
of the desk.

416
00:20:41,699 --> 00:20:42,825
[high-pitched note]

417
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:44,744
You understand my theory?

418
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:46,620
-[LAHAN] Indeed.
-[BOTH] Mm.

419
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:51,208
[MAOMAO] Finally, that silver
fluid she drank at the end.

420
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:54,044
That was mercury.

421
00:20:54,128 --> 00:20:55,254
It is poison.

422
00:20:56,130 --> 00:20:58,132
I don't know
if she actually drank it,

423
00:20:58,215 --> 00:20:59,341
but no human should.

424
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,886
You should find
a chance to explain that all

425
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:03,304
to the high-ranking officials.

426
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:06,182
♪

427
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:10,770
A few days after the show,

428
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:14,231
the White Lady vanished
into thin air, without a trace.

429
00:21:15,441 --> 00:21:16,817
The only sign that remained

430
00:21:16,901 --> 00:21:18,777
was a mysterious chain
of food poisonings

431
00:21:18,861 --> 00:21:20,738
among the merchants in the city.

432
00:21:22,156 --> 00:21:24,283
What was that
white serpentine sorceress

433
00:21:24,366 --> 00:21:26,035
trying to achieve
with her performance?

434
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:30,998
Mercury, when inhaled as a vapor
or when bound to something else,

435
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:33,542
is highly toxic
to living creatures.

436
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:39,173
But occasionally,
it can be used as medicine too.

437
00:21:47,765 --> 00:21:50,017
Poison, medicine.

438
00:21:51,101 --> 00:21:52,728
It's all about the intent.

439
00:22:15,584 --> 00:22:17,545
[♪ closing theme song playing]

440
00:23:48,594 --> 00:23:51,096
♪

441
00:23:53,807 --> 00:23:56,769
[NARRATOR]
Next time, "The Paper Village."

